    "timing_convention_reconciliation": "All candidate and opponent faults were timeout (>50 ms) strikes on individual turns in n09 and n10. In runner.py, a reply that misses the 50 ms deadline increments faults and stale count. If the line is subsequently retrieved after timeout, it is recorded in self.late; if the queue was empty when polled or the reply was consumed stale on the next turn, faults is incremented while late stays 0. Furthermore, max_ms in the JSON summary is computed strictly over self.latencies (replies that arrived in time), which is why max_ms is reported as <50 ms even in games with a timeout strike."
  },
